{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s22-p01-01",
      "text": "If you get angry many times in a day,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p01-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p01-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p01-02",
      "text": "it is time for you to think about how to deal with it.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p01-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p01-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p02",
      "text": "Here are some of my suggestions.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p03",
      "text": "When you are angry, try to tell yourself through another voice that you are angry and that it is okay.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p04",
      "text": "You don't need to punish yourself for being angry.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p05",
      "text": "It just shows that you have different ideas.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p06",
      "text": "Accept that many things are not 100% right or wrong.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p07-01",
      "text": "In our communication with others, the final purpose is not to decide who is right,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p07-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p07-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p07-02",
      "text": "but to look for something in common and agree on a solution.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p07-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p07-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p08",
      "text": "If you still feel strong anger, it is advised that you try going for a jog to let anger out.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p09",
      "text": "Wearing a comfortable cotton blouse can also help you feel more relaxed.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p10",
      "text": "It's useful to make a promise to yourself to manage anger.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p11",
      "text": "Just like building wealth by saving every cent, small efforts can lead to big improvements.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p12-01",
      "text": "Don't shout or say angry words when you are very angry,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p12-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p12-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p12-02",
      "text": "for you will regret saying them when you cool down and may have to say sorry later.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p12-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p12-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p13",
      "text": "Discussing with a third party is helpful.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p14-01",
      "text": "It is hard for the two parties in anger to understand each other,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p14-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p14-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p14-02",
      "text": "but the idea of an outsider can help both parties to get mutual understanding.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p14-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p14-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p15-01",
      "text": "Managing your anger is like letting a horse run in a field,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p15-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p15-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p15-02",
      "text": "which means you need to find ways to release the tension.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p15-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p15-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p16",
      "text": "Anger is just one of the many emotions that make us human.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22-p17",
      "text": "And managing it well adds to our ability to truly understand the world.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s22-p17.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
